<p>Once the car is secured on the ramp, <em>individual steel wheel‑lock chocks</em> are positioned behind each tire. These high‑strength chocks clamp onto the wheel hub, preventing rotational movement even when the vehicle is subjected to the vibration and lateral forces typical of highway travel.</p>
<p>The chocks are made from alloy steel and are fitted with anti‑slip pads to ensure a firm grip on the ramp surface.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">To guarantee that the vehicle remains stationary during transit, <em>high‑tensile ratchet lashing</em> is applied around the chassis and the car’s frame.</p>
